# Line endings are LF everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# There was no policy here, and core.autocrlf is set to true on at least one
# machine, so whether a file arrived as LF or CRLF depended on who checked it
# out. That is not cosmetic. The markdown parsers find the first paragraph by
# splitting on a blank line, and /\n{2,}/ cannot match \r\n\r\n because of the
# carriage return between the newlines — so a CRLF file parses as one enormous
# paragraph.
#
# It shipped. One reference page served its own citation, publisher included, as
# its search snippet, and the same fault was latent in the hub previews and in
# the summary handed to every AI crawler through llms.txt. The parsers now
# normalise their input, which fixes the symptom; this fixes the cause, so a
# checkout on any machine produces the bytes the parsers were written against.
*               text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets, never touched.
*.png           binary
*.ico           binary
*.mp3           binary
*.m4a           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
